  data: {
    LLM: 'Remove one queen to start the tableau. As further queens appear during the deal, each starts a new column. Place all fives and sixes to the foundations when available; build fives downward to aces and kings, and sixes upward to jacks, regardless of suit. Move top cards from tableau and stock to legal foundation positions.',
    Player: 'Remove one queen to start the tableau. As further queens appear during the deal, each starts a new column. Place all fives and sixes to the foundations when available; build fives downward to aces and kings, and sixes upward to jacks, regardless of suit. Move top cards from tableau and stock to legal foundation positions.',
    objective: 'Move all cards from the two decks onto the foundations, using the queen tableau columns and the paired five and six foundations without exhausting legal moves.',
    gameplay: 'Remove one queen to start the tableau. As further queens appear during the deal, each starts a new column. Place all fives and sixes to the foundations when available; build fives downward to aces and kings, and sixes upward to jacks, regardless of suit. Move top cards from tableau and stock to legal foundation positions.',
    keyRules: [
      'Eight queens become tableau column bases.',
      'Fives build downward and sixes build upward regardless of suit.',
      'The game uses two full decks.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
