    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 0 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Move all cards from the two decks onto the foundations, using the queen tableau columns and the paired five and six foundations without exhausting legal moves.',
      'Turn-flow example: Remove one queen to start the tableau. As further queens appear during the deal, each starts a new column. Place all fives and sixes to the foundations when available; build fives downward to aces and kings, and sixes upward to jacks, regardless of suit. Move top cards from tableau and stock to legal foundation positions.',
      'Scoring example: The game is won only by completing all foundations; otherwise the deal is lost when the stock is exhausted. Complete all eight foundations, four building up from ace to king and four building down from king to ace, without regard to suit..',
